{"t":1794364851853,"type":"say","kind":"approval","why":"The reply stops before spending credits and asks \"Shall I go ahead like that?\" It asks the user to confirm a plan that costs about 15 credits. It also asks for a short clip description and a choice between two options, but the main ask is confirmation to proceed with the spend.","called":true,"text":"Before I spend any credits, I need to flag two problems with this request.\n\n1. I can't watch the video. None of my tools let me view video frames or hear the audio. All I could check is that it shows three people's faces at the start and one later on. That isn't enough to write a narration that explains what's going on.\n\n2. I can't swap the soundtrack and keep the footage unchanged. Magic Hour has no tool that just replaces a video's audio track. The closest one is lip-sync, but it changes the speakers' mouth movements, so the footage wouldn't stay as it is. Any other video tool would re-render the clip.\n\nHere's what I can do:\n- You send me one or two sentences on what happens in the clip (who's there, what they're doing, where it is). I write a short, friendly, matter-of-fact narration, about 25 words to fit 10 seconds.\n- I turn it into a 10-second English voice-over audio file with a clear, neutral voice. It costs about 15 credits.\n- You put that audio on the video yourself in any basic editor (CapCut, iMovie, Clipchamp): mute the original track and drop in the new one. The footage stays exactly as it is, with no music or captions.\n\nShall I go ahead like that? If you'd rather use lip-sync and accept the mouth changes, tell me and I'll do that."}
{"t":1794364851854,"type":"user","text":"Yes, go ahead."}
